## Critical Safety Rules

These rules are NON-NEGOTIABLE. Claude Code must NEVER violate them:

- NEVER run `terraform destroy` or `terraform apply -auto-approve` in production
- NEVER execute `kubectl delete namespace` in any environment
- NEVER commit secrets, tokens, or credentials to version control
- NEVER modify production resources without a plan file and explicit approval
- NEVER bypass GitOps — all production changes go through [ArgoCD/Flux]
- NEVER scale production to zero without incident commander approval
- ALWAYS use `--dry-run=client` before any mutating kubectl command in prod
- ALWAYS verify the current kubectl context before running commands
- ALWAYS check terraform workspace/state before plan or apply

